Local patch on top of upstream 8edb2b66cb2da969d54ece257d0a81047f5f8c8e.

yt-dlp preflight: --hooks, --transcribe and --download shell out to the yt-dlp
command-line tool, which requirements.txt does not install. Without this check
each per-video probe fails on its own, the run prints one warning per video and
then writes a workbook with empty hook columns — after spending the search quota.
With it, the run stops before the first API call with exit code 6 and prints the
right install command for the platform.

Written by Nicole 2026-09-18. Submitted upstream 2026-09-24 as
https://github.com/AgriciDaniel/youtube-scout/pull/1 (with tests and a CHANGELOG
entry). If it merges, drop this patch at the next re-vendor instead of
re-applying it.

Reapply after a re-vendor:  cd vendor/youtube-scout && patch -p1 < patches/0001-ytdlp-preflight.patch

